#: src/ai/mcp.md:3
msgid "Model Context Protocol"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:5
msgid ""
"Zed uses the [Model Context Protocol](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/) to "
"interact with context servers."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:7
msgid ""
"The Model Context Protocol (MCP) is an open protocol for connecting LLM "
"applications to external tools and data sources through a standard interface."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:9
msgid "Supported Features"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:11
msgid ""
"Zed currently supports MCP's [Tools](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/"
"specification/2025-11-25/server/tools) and [Prompts](https://"
"modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/server/prompts) features. "
"We welcome contributions that help advance Zed's MCP feature coverage "
"(Discovery, Sampling, Elicitation, etc)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:14
msgid ""
"Zed also handles the `notifications/tools/list_changed` notification from "
"MCP servers. When a server adds, removes, or modifies its available tools at "
"runtime, Zed automatically reloads the tool list without requiring a server "
"restart."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:16
msgid "Installing MCP Servers"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:18
msgid "As Extensions"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:20
msgid ""
"One of the ways you can use MCP servers in Zed is by exposing them as an "
"extension. Check out the [MCP Server Extensions](../extensions/mcp-"
"extensions.md) page to learn how to create your own."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:23
msgid "Many MCP servers are available as extensions. Find them via:"
