#: src/ai/mcp.md:64
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can also add a custom server by accessing the Agent "
"Panel's Settings view (also accessible via the `agent: open settings` "
"action). From there, you can add it through the modal that appears when you "
"click the \"Add Custom Server\" button."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:67
msgid ""
"Note: When a remote MCP server has no configured `\"Authorization\"` header, "
"Zed will prompt you to authenticate yourself against the MCP server using "
"the standard MCP OAuth flow."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:69
msgid "Using MCP Servers"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:71
msgid "Configuration Check"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:73
msgid "Most MCP servers require configuration after installation."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:75
msgid ""
"In the case of extensions, after installing it, Zed will pop up a modal "
"displaying what is required for you to properly set it up. For example, the "
"GitHub MCP extension requires you to add a [Personal Access Token](https://"
"docs.github.com/en/authentication/keeping-your-account-and-data-secure/"
"managing-your-personal-access-tokens)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:78
msgid ""
"In the case of custom servers, make sure you check the provider "
"documentation to determine what type of command, arguments, and environment "
"variables need to be added to the JSON."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:80
msgid ""
"To check if your MCP server is properly configured, go to the Agent Panel's "
"settings view and watch the indicator dot next to its name. If they're "
"running correctly, the indicator will be green and its tooltip will say "
"\"Server is active\". If not, other colors and tooltip messages will "
"indicate what is happening."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:84
msgid "Agent Panel Usage"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:86
msgid ""
"Once installation is complete, you can return to the Agent Panel and start "
"prompting."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:88
msgid ""
"How reliably MCP tools get called can vary from model to model. Mentioning "
"the MCP server by name can help the model pick tools from that server."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:91
msgid ""
"However, if you want to _ensure_ a given MCP server will be used, you can "
"create [a custom profile](./agent-panel.md#custom-profiles) where all built-"
"in tools (or the ones that could cause conflicts with the server's tools) "
"are turned off and only the tools coming from the MCP server are turned on."
msgstr ""

